---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/layout/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="Now" description="What I'm working on right now, and the numbers coming out of the systems that are running.">
<style>
  .head { padding: 56px 0 0; max-width: 46rem; }
  .head p { color: var(--text-2); margin-top: 8px; }
  .stamp { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--text-3); margin-top: 10px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

  .work { margin-top: 40px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 22px 40px; }
  .item { border-top: 2px solid var(--amber); padding-top: 16px; }
  .item h3 { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .item .state { font-size: .74rem; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-3); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .item p { color: var(--text-2); font-size: .95rem; }
  .item a { color: var(--amber); }
  .item a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  .statgrid { margin-top: 22px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: rgba(196,151,42,.15); border: 1px solid rgba(196,151,42,.15); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; }
  .stat { background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0e0e0c, #0a0a09); padding: 24px 24px 20px; display: block; }
  a.stat:hover { background: linear-gradient(180deg, #14130f, #0d0d0b); }
  .stat .n { display: block; font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 2.1rem; line-height: 1.05; color: var(--amber); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .stat .l { display: block; font-size: .86rem; color: var(--text-2); margin-top: 6px; }
  .stat .s { display: block; font-size: .76rem; color: var(--text-3); margin-top: 2px; }

  .stale { margin-top: 14px; font-size: .84rem; color: var(--text-3); max-width: 62ch; }
  .latest { margin-top: 22px; max-width: 46rem; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .work { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 26px; } }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .statgrid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
</style>

<Nav variant="full" active="/now" />

<main class="wrapb">
  <div class="head">
    <h1 class="statement">Now</h1>
    <p>What I'm working on, and what the running systems are saying.</p>
    <p class="stamp">Updated 9 September 2026</p>
  </div>

  <div class="work">
    <div class="item">
      <h3>Puttfor</h3>
      <div class="state">Live</div>
      <p>Charity golf, run properly. Registration, payments and live scoring in one place: the leaderboard updates while groups are still on the course, and the money lands in the event's own Stripe account rather than the course's. <a href="https://puttfor.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">puttfor.com →</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="item">
      <h3>agentic-id</h3>
      <div class="state">Building</div>
      <p>Intent tokens. An agent should be able to prove <em>why</em> it is acting, not just that it holds a valid credential. Built on RFC 8693 and SPIFFE rather than a new format, because the primitives already exist. Next: a reference implementation clean enough to open source.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="item">
      <h3>Commonlist</h3>
      <div class="state">Live, still hardening</div>
      <p>One address book merged out of Google, Microsoft, Outlook and iCloud. It works; moving it off test auth credentials is the job before it gets real traffic. <a href="https://commonlist.matterunknown.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try it →</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="item">
      <h3>Harvest Haven</h3>
      <div class="state">Weekends</div>
      <p>A Roblox farming game I'm building with my 10 year old. Crop chains, pets, and an economy he keeps redesigning.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sect">
    <div class="sect-head"><h2>The models, by the numbers</h2><a href="/projects">All projects →</a></div>
    <div class="statgrid">
      <a class="stat" href="/projects/pokemon-model">
        <span class="n" data-stat="pokemon-cards">17,428</span>
        <span class="l">Pokémon cards scored</span>
        <span class="s">across <span data-stat="pokemon-sets">168</span> sets</span>
      </a>
      <a class="stat" href="/projects/gpk-model">
        <span class="n" data-stat="gpk-cards">11,580</span>
        <span class="l">Garbage Pail Kids tracked</span>
        <span class="s">114 sets, 1985-2025</span>
      </a>
      <a class="stat" href="/projects/onepiece-model">
        <span class="n" data-stat="onepiece-cards">1,035</span>
        <span class="l">One Piece cards scored</span>
        <span class="s">43 sets</span>
      </a>
      <a class="stat" href="/projects/quant-trading">
        <span class="n" data-stat="quant-positions">8</span>
        <span class="l">Open positions</span>
        <span class="s">100 symbols scanned nightly · paper</span>
      </a>
      <a class="stat" href="/projects/crypto-model">
        <span class="n" data-stat="crypto-assets">21</span>
        <span class="l">Crypto assets scored daily</span>
        <span class="s"><span data-stat="crypto-buys">0</span> buy signals</span>
      </a>
      <a class="stat" href="/projects/identity-map">
        <span class="n">12</span>
        <span class="l">Systems in the identity map</span>
        <span class="s">that hold a version of you</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="stale">These come out of the nightly model runs. The job last pushed on <span data-stat="asof">19 August 2026</span>, so that is the date these numbers are from. Getting the pipeline running again is on the list. When it is, this page updates itself.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="sect">
    <div class="sect-head"><h2>Latest writing</h2><a href="/writing">All writing →</a></div>
    <div class="latest">
      <a class="wrow" href="/writing/retiring-vessel"><span class="wt">Retiring Vessel</span><span class="wd">Aug 2026</span></a>
      <a class="wrow" href="/writing/the-credential-remembers-who"><span class="wt">The Credential Remembers Who. Nothing Remembers Why.</span><span class="wd">Jul 2026</span></a>
      <a class="wrow" href="/writing/the-workload-is-the-reasoning-session"><span class="wt">The Workload Is the Reasoning Session</span><span class="wd">Jul 2026</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<Footer />
</Base>
